Thoery 
GitHub is a version control platform used to store and manage source code. Jenkins integrates with GitHub to automatically build and 
test software whenever code changes are pushed to the repository. This improves software quality and reduces manual effort.

1. Create a GitHub repository and upload the software project.
2. Configure GitHub credentials and the repository URL in Jenkins.
3. Create a Jenkins Pipeline job and configure the source code repository.
4. Create a `Jenkinsfile` containing build and testing stages.
5. Configure a GitHub webhook to trigger Jenkins automatically on code changes.
6. Execute the pipeline and verify the build and test results.
